{
 "version": 1,
 "method": {
  "extraction": "MediaPipe Hands, Tasks API HandLandmarker (mediapipe 1.1.0, hand_landmarker.task float16), IMAGE mode (every sampled frame independent, no tracking), num_hands=2, min detection/presence confidence 0.5. Frames sampled at 6 fps over the downloaded section. Per detection: handedness label+score, 21 image landmarks, 21 world landmarks (metres, hand-centred).",
  "quality_gate": "kept if handedness score >= 0.8, image bbox diagonal >= 70 px, and the summed PIP+DIP flexion of fingers 2-5 under the reported handedness is >= -20 deg (all four fingers bent backwards = mirror/chirality garbage). Rejected counts per reason are in each source.",
  "measures": "see blockout/human_score.py MEASURES; identical code runs on the MediaPipe world landmarks and on the anim joint chains",
  "pooling": "finger measures (mcp/pip/dip/tip_pitch) pool fingers 2-5. Pooled percentiles weight each video by min(kept hand-frames, 300). per_video bands are unweighted. per_finger and splits bands are unweighted over all kept hand-frames.",
  "pressing_vs_free": "MediaPipe cannot tell which finger is pressing. Split \"lowest\" = the finger (2-5) whose tip reaches furthest palmward of the palm plane in that hand-frame (contact proxy), \"others\" = the rest. Informational only.",
  "reliability": [
   "World landmarks are a learned 3D estimate; occluded fingers (far side of the hand in side views, fingers under the palm in overhead views) are inferred from the network prior, not seen.",
   "Cross-check on side-view clips: unsigned PIP+DIP from world landmarks vs from 2D image landmarks correlate r=0.78 (6Yn39pyPK-Q) and 0.82 (GLIz7feMlvE); 2D is smaller as expected from projection, so world landmarks are not flattening the fingers relative to what the image shows. Correlation drops to 0.2-0.5 on overhead and three-quarter clips, where 2D angles are foreshortened and say little.",
   "Motion blur in fast passages (hjwgza1-gF8 middle section, wevdC1YiN4c, RlCLUpaOluE) gives sliver/flat skeletons; most are dropped by the handedness-score gate (low score), not all.",
   "Reflections in the fallboard/lid produced a few detections (jEuj-XD0MqM); they are mirror images and mostly fail the chirality gate.",
   "Side views (6Yn, hjwg, GLIz, rZz) read systematically flatter (PIP p50 10-17 deg) than overhead/three-quarter views (gFPSH, jEuj, apxsca: 24-33 deg). Part is the players (GLIz and wevdC play with visibly flat, extended fingers), part may be view-dependent bias; the pooled band spans both.",
   "Wrist height vs knuckles cannot be measured from world landmarks (no gravity direction); it is only in the qualitative notes.",
   "Thumb landmarks are the least reliable: the thumb is hidden under the hand in most side views."
  ],
  "tip_definition": "MediaPipe tip = fingertip (skin end); anim tip = end of the distal bone. Only angles/ratios are compared.",
  "extract_script": "\"\"\"Extract MediaPipe hand landmarks from videos at a fixed sample rate.\"\"\"\nimport sys, json, os, cv2, numpy as np\nimport mediapipe as mp\nfrom mediapipe.tasks import python as mpt\nfrom mediapipe.tasks.python import vision\n\nMODEL = '/tmp/claude-1000/humanref/model/hand_landmarker.task'\nFPS = float(os.environ.get('SFPS', '6'))\n\ndef main(video, out_json, frames_dir):\n    os.makedirs(frames_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    opts = vision.HandLandmarkerOptions(\n        base_options=mpt.BaseOptions(model_asset_path=MODEL),\n        running_mode=vision.RunningMode.IMAGE, num_hands=2,\n        min_hand_detection_confidence=0.5, min_hand_presence_confidence=0.5)\n    det = vision.HandLandmarker.create_from_options(opts)\n    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(video)\n    vfps = cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FPS); n = int(cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_COUNT))\n    step = vfps / FPS\n    recs = []; k = 0; nxt = 0.0; idx = 0; nsampled = 0\n    while True:\n        ok, fr = cap.read()\n        if not ok: break\n        if idx + 1e-6 >= nxt:\n            nxt += step; nsampled += 1\n            t = idx / vfps\n            rgb = cv2.cvtColor(fr, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n            res = det.detect(mp.Image(image_format=mp.ImageFormat.SRGB, data=rgb))\n            H, W = fr.shape[:2]\n            for h in range(len(res.hand_landmarks)):\n                im = np.array([[p.x * W, p.y * H, p.z * W] for p in res.hand_landmarks[h]])\n                wl = np.array([[p.x, p.y, p.z] for p in res.hand_world_landmarks[h]])\n                hd = res.handedness[h][0]\n                bb = [float(im[:, 0].min()), float(im[:, 1].min()), float(im[:, 0].max()), float(im[:, 1].max())]\n                recs.append(dict(t=round(t, 3), frame=idx, label=hd.category_name, score=round(hd.score, 4),\n                                 bbox=[round(b, 1) for b in bb], img=im.round(2).tolist(), world=wl.round(5).tolist()))\n            if res.hand_landmarks and k % 15 == 0:\n                vis = fr.copy()\n                for h in range(len(res.hand_landmarks)):\n                    pts = [(int(p.x * W), int(p.y * H)) for p in res.hand_landmarks[h]]\n                    for a, b in [(0,1),(1,2),(2,3),(3,4),(0,5),(5,6),(6,7),(7,8),(0,9),(9,10),(10,11),(11,12),(0,13),(13,14),(14,15),(15,16),(0,17),(17,18),(18,19),(19,20),(5,9),(9,13),(13,17)]:\n                        cv2.line(vis, pts[a], pts[b], (0, 255, 0), 1)\n                cv2.imwrite(os.path.join(frames_dir, f'{t:07.2f}.jpg'), vis)\n                cv2.imwrite(os.path.join(frames_dir, f'{t:07.2f}_raw.jpg'), fr)\n            if res.hand_landmarks: k += 1\n        idx += 1\n    json.dump(dict(video=os.path.basename(video), vfps=vfps, sample_fps=FPS, n_sampled=nsampled,\n                   size=[int(cap.get(3)), int(cap.get(4))], dets=recs), open(out_json, 'w'))\n    print(os.path.basename(video), 'sampled', nsampled, 'dets', len(recs))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main(*sys.argv[1:4])\n",
  "download": "yt-dlp -f \"bv*[height<=720][ext=mp4]/bv*[height<=720]\" --download-sections \"*0-300\"; footage kept local only (not committed)",
  "visual_qa": "Annotated frames (every 15th frame with a detection, up to 30 per video) rated GOOD/PARTIAL/BAD per skeleton by Haiku reviewers; placement-level, generous; spot-checked at full resolution by the builder (overruled for wiLlFnWFNck)."
 },
 "qualitative": [
  "Fingers are curved over the keys in most frames of the overhead and three-quarter clips (apxscaNxwuU, gFPSH8nBJyo, jEuj-XD0MqM); a minority of players (GLIz7feMlvE, wevdC1YiN4c) play with flat, extended fingers.",
  "Wrist is about level with the knuckles in essentially every side-view frame inspected (6Yn39pyPK-Q, hjwgza1-gF8, GLIz7feMlvE, J56sx69a1VI, jEuj-XD0MqM); not dropped below the key line, not humped high.",
  "Free fingers hover just above the keys; whole-hand lifts happen between chords (hjwgza1-gF8 chord section, hands raised with fingers arched).",
  "Thumb, where visible (overhead RlCLUpaOluE, Pianote close-ups), lies extended along the keys, angled out from the hand, playing on its side; it is rarely tucked under.",
  "Left-hand fingers often bunched together over neighbouring keys (gFPSH8nBJyo); on chords the hand opens with the thumb and pinky splayed (RlCLUpaOluE, hjwgza1-gF8).",
  "Pianote lesson (rZznie6UU_o, qualitative only, excluded from the numbers) teaches rounded fingers, contact near the fingertip, wrist level with the knuckles, and shows flat fingers as the fault."
 ],
